{title: Buffalo Gals}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: G}

{c: Verse 1}
As [G]I was walking down the street, down the street, down the street,
A [D7]pretty girl I chanced to meet, oh [G]she was fair to see.

{c: Chorus}
[G]Buffalo gals, won't you come out tonight, come out tonight, come out tonight,
[G]Buffalo gals, won't you [D7]come out tonight and [G]dance by the light of the moon?

{c: Verse 2}
I [G]asked her if she'd stop and talk, stop and talk, stop and talk,
Her [D7]feet covered up the whole sidewalk, [G]she was fair to see.

{c: Verse 3}
I [G]danced with a gal with a hole in her stocking, hole in her stocking,
And her [D7]heel kept a-rocking, and her [G]toes kept a-knocking,
I [G]danced with a gal with a [D7]hole in her stocking, [G]we danced by the light of the moon.
